        "original_id": "c3355bf3-ec98-503d-8d21-b504b2c01555",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Boyle, Danny Arnold, Michael Cavanaugh\n- TV Shows: Joe Bash, Barney Miller, The X-Files, The West Wing, Starman, Hunter, Monk, 24\n- Films: Joe\n- Organizations: New York City Police Department\n- Roles: TV producer, beat cop, police detective\n\nFacts:\n- In 1970, Peter Boyle had a breakthrough performance in the film \"Joe\".\n- After his breakthrough in \"Joe,\" Peter Boyle won praise in both comedic and dramatic roles.\n- Danny Arnold created the TV series \"Joe Bash\" after his successful New York City police detective sitcom \"Barney Miller\".\n- \"Joe Bash\" starred Peter Boyle as a weary and embittered New York City Police Department beat cop.\n- In 1996, Peter Boyle won an Emmy Award for a guest-starring role on the science-fiction drama \"The X-Files\".\n- Michael Cavanaugh had television guest credits including \"The West Wing,\" \"Joe Bash,\" \"Starman,\" \"Hunter,\" \"Monk,\" and \"24\".",
